    "['ipv6 unicast-routing', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you\\'re using Junos OS versions that support the more direct IPv6 routing enablement:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact equivalent in Juniper depends on the context. The first option creates the IPv6 routing table, while the second enables IPv6 routing through router advertisements. For a direct equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"ipv6 unicast-routing\" that simply enables IPv6 routing globally, you would typically use:\\n\\n##\\nset routing-options autonomous-system 1\\nset routing-options forwarding-table export EXPORT_NAME\\n##\\n\\nBut the simplest form that enables IPv6 routing is implicit in Juniper - IPv6 routing is enabled by default when you configure IPv6 interfaces.', 'trans_template': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you\\'re using Junos OS versions that support the more direct IPv6 routing enablement:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact equivalent in Juniper depends on the context. The first option creates the IPv6 routing table, while the second enables IPv6 routing through router advertisements. For a direct equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"ipv6 unicast-routing\" that simply enables IPv6 routing globally, you would typically use:\\n\\n##\\nset routing-options autonomous-system 1\\nset routing-options forwarding-table export EXPORT_NAME\\n##\\n\\nBut the simplest form that enables IPv6 routing is implicit in